# Milestone: v0.10.10-job-introspection
# Covers: spawning 100 detached strands via detach(); each increments counter
#         twice with a 1s sleep in between; final value is 200 after 2s wait.
#
# Rewritten from legacy tests/2.x/detach-many.chk for the host driver.
# Named-function declarations are not parsed, so `add2` is a `var`
# holding a function; `x++` and the C-style `for` are spelled out.  All
# hundred first increments land before any sleeper wakes; one unbudgeted
# step after the clock passes the one-second sleep finishes all hundred.
## timeout: 30
## host: run var x = 0
## host: run var add2 = function() { x = x + 1; sleep(1s); x = x + 1 }
## host: run var i = 0; while (i < 100) { detach(add2()); i = i + 1 }; i
## host: run x
## host: advance-clock 1000
## host: step 0
## host: run x
## host: live-work
# matrix-row: separator-detach
[00000000] 0
[00000000] <?>
[00000000] 100
[00000000] 100
[00000000] step: QUIESCENT
[00000000] 200
[00000000] live-work: false
